@startuml SherpaSignUpClassDiagram
title Sherpa — Sign-up Data Model
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

note top
  IMPLEMENTED SCOPE: sign-up only
  IDs are String values generated as UUIDs for SQLite/Prisma.
  User.role is stored as a String (student, teacher, employer).
  Major and desired career are student-only optional profile fields.
  Require both during student sign-up validation; Prisma cannot express
  this role-dependent requirement in the schema alone.
end note

package "Sign-up entities" {
  class User {
    +id: String <<PK, uuid>>
    +email: String <<unique, required>>
    +passwordHash: String <<required>>
    +firstName: String <<required>>
    +lastName: String <<required>>
    +role: String <<required>>
    +createdAt: DateTime <<required>>
  }

  class Profile {
    +userId: String <<PK, FK>>
    +majorProgramId: String? <<FK, student only>>
    +desiredCareerId: String? <<FK, student only>>
  }

  class Program {
    +id: String <<PK, uuid>>
    +name: String <<unique, required>>
  }

  class CareerField {
    +id: String <<PK, uuid>>
    +name: String <<unique, required>>
  }
}

User "1" -- "0..1" Profile : has
Program "0..1" <-- "0..*" Profile : selected major
CareerField "0..1" <-- "0..*" Profile : desired career

note bottom
  Sign-up form values: email, first name, last name, classification (role),
  and password. Student sign-ups additionally require major and desired career.
  The password is stored as a hash on User.
  Profile fields not collected during sign-up are intentionally excluded.
end note
@enduml
